==Strategy==
[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] are excellent choices. Ramen is a great tank, even holding up well against the Cyberhorns and Cli-One. Seafarer is an excellent [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] crowd-controller (especially with [[Talents]]) and produces good damage. Can Can is all around great, especially with the Target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] Talent.

What usually happens in most cases is that Cli-One will stay behind Clionel and guard her blind spot, damaging and occasionally weakening your cats. This isn't so much of a threat as it is an annoyance, as Cli-One is only at her [[Uncanny Legends]] magnification (1,600%).

The Lutrinae Gokurakkos are the real threat here, as they are tanky and have a chance of knocking back your cat units into Clionel's range, screwing up everything. Have a counter to deal with them or disable them of their knockback through curse.

The Cyberhorns are VERY tanky and just act as unbreakable walls to slowly push your units. Bring some high DPS units to get rid of them quickly.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Can easily rush down either of the backline enemies or supporting Cyberhorns. To ensure maximum damage, use either Thunderbolt or Curseblast.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: A powerful melee attacker who can clear peons and do significant damage to the Cyberhorns. If close enough, the [[Wave Attack]]s can even reach the two backline enemies.

==Trivia==
*The [[wikipedia:Hadal zone|hadal zone]] is the deepest zone of the ocean, extending below 6,000 meters (20,000 feet).

